%description:

RFC 826 -- a host that answered a request needs no request of its own.

Checks RFC826-RECV-6 and RFC826-RECV-7 from
doc/project/evidence/standard/rfc826/catalog.md. The English procedure is in
doc/project/evidence/protocol/arp/checks/reply.md#learning-from-a-request; the program steps
below map onto its expected observations. Mapping of the pair mockup: host A = hostA,
host B = hostB.

Host A resolves the address of host B at 0.1 s. Host B then sends its own datagram to
host A at 0.5 s. Host B has never asked for the address of host A, so the only place its
table entry can have come from is the sender fields of the request of host A -- which the
reception algorithm reads before it reads the opcode.

The two hosts use two ports, 5000 for the datagrams of host A and 6000 for the datagram of
host B, so that a step cannot match the wrong datagram.

Deviation: expected observation 2, that the datagram of host B reaches host A, is not a
program step. The absence watch of expected observation 3 has to cover the moment at 0.5 s
when host B needs the hardware address of host A, and a greedy step consumes its whole
window, so a later step would look for the datagram after it had already arrived. The
delivery is asserted instead on the line that the receiving program prints at the end of the
run.

The absence watch runs from the reply of host B to the end of the run. The one window it
does not cover is the start of the run before the reply, and in it host B has nothing to
send and therefore no address to resolve.

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "ArpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("rfc826_learning_from_request")
        // Expected observation 1: the request of host A, and the reply of host B.
        .once(on("hostA.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .packet("arp.opcode == 1")
                  .describe("the request from host A")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("hostB.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .packet("arp.opcode == 2")
                  .describe("host B's reply")
                  .within(0.1))
        // Expected observation 3: host B never asks for the address of host A, although it
        // sends a datagram to host A at 0.5 s (RFC826-RECV-6, RECV-7).
        .never(on("hostB.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .packet("arp.opcode == 1")
                  .describe("an ARP request from host B")
                  .within(0.85));
}

%activity:
// present only so opp_test compiles the %global above; this module is not in the network.
EV << "rfc826_learning_from_request compiled\n";

%file: test.ned

import inet.node.ethernet.Eth100M;
import inet.node.inet.StandardHost;
import inet.networklayer.configurator.ipv4.Ipv4NetworkConfigurator;

// The pair mockup: two hosts on one Ethernet link.
network ArpPairNet
{
    submodules:
        configurator: Ipv4NetworkConfigurator { @display("p=100,50"); }
        hostA: StandardHost { @display("p=300,100"); }
        hostB: StandardHost { @display("p=500,100"); }
    connections:
        hostA.ethg++ <--> Eth100M <--> hostB.ethg++; // link 1
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
network = ArpPairNet
sim-time-limit = 1s
seed-set = 0

# Host A: one datagram to port 5000 of host B at 0.1 s, and a program on port 6000.
*.hostA.numApps = 2
*.hostA.app[0].typename = "UdpBasicApp"
*.hostA.app[0].destAddresses = "hostB"
*.hostA.app[0].destPort = 5000
*.hostA.app[0].localPort = 4000
*.hostA.app[0].messageLength = 100B
*.hostA.app[0].startTime = 0.1s
*.hostA.app[0].sendInterval = 1s
*.hostA.app[1].typename = "UdpSink"
*.hostA.app[1].localPort = 6000

# Host B: a program on port 5000, and one datagram to port 6000 of host A at 0.5 s.
*.hostB.numApps = 2
*.hostB.app[0].typename = "UdpSink"
*.hostB.app[0].localPort = 5000
*.hostB.app[1].typename = "UdpBasicApp"
*.hostB.app[1].destAddresses = "hostA"
*.hostB.app[1].destPort = 6000
*.hostB.app[1].localPort = 4001
*.hostB.app[1].messageLength = 100B
*.hostB.app[1].startTime = 0.5s
*.hostB.app[1].sendInterval = 1s

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST rfc826_learning_from_request: PASS

%contains: stdout
hostA.app[1]: received 1 packets
